; atc_return.ngc - Return the current tool to its carousel pocket
;
; Called by flexihal_atc.c tool_change() when the requested tool is NOT
; in the carousel but the current tool IS.  The machine returns the
; current tool to its pocket, then atc_pause.ngc takes over for the
; manual swap.
;
; Parameters passed via numbered parameters:
;   #1 = carousel pocket number to return the tool to (P word)
;
; Note: no $TCMEASURE here — that is handled by atc_pause.ngc which
; runs immediately after this macro completes.

M5    ; ensure spindle is off
M9    ; ensure coolant is off

; ── Calculate return pocket XY ───────────────────────────────────────────────
; Adjust to match your carousel geometry (same formula as atc_change.ngc)
#100 = [50.0 + [#1 - 1] * 40.0]    ; pocket X = x_pocket_1 + (pocket-1) * offset
#101 = 200.0                         ; pocket Y (fixed for linear carousel)

; ── Retract to safe Z ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
G53 G0 Z#<_home_z>

; ── Move to return pocket XY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
G53 G0 X#100 Y#101

; ── Descend and release tool into pocket ─────────────────────────────────────
G53 G0 Z#<_atc_z_start>
G53 G1 Z#<_atc_z_engage> F#<_atc_feed>

$DRBO                                ; open drawbar — release tool into pocket
G4 P0.5                              ; dwell for drawbar to fully open

G53 G0 Z#<_home_z>                  ; retract with empty spindle

M2
